implementationPlan.description:
Case (a), the unmerged half of the L2 union. Edit scripts/tests/postflight-worktree.cjs only, with the Edit tool.

Placement (governor comment-943c6629: task-e3e81c45 adds cases to this file too): put the new function directly after `async function wtResume(){...}` (it ends just before the markerScan comment block, about :1149). Register it in the case table right after `'wt-resume':wtResume,` on the existing line (:1550), never at the end of the file or of the table.

`async function wtResumeUnmerged()`. Head it with a 2-line comment: a non-conflict unlanded route stores no paths, so the resume's conflict is outside landingRetry.paths, and only the `--diff-filter=U` half of the scan can catch its markers.
- p = repo('wt-resume-unmerged', {settings: {...LANDS, qualityGate: gateCmd()}}). log = path.join(root, 'wt-resume-unmerged-gate.jsonl').
- landRun(p, 'wt-resume-unmerged-0', {'src/a.txt': 'task a\n'}): a checkpoint T.
- landRun(p, 'wt-resume-unmerged-1', {}, {...REVIEW, WT_GATE_LOG: log, WT_GATE_EXIT: '3'}): MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_GATE, routed unlanded. Assert retryOf(p).reason === 'gate' and deepEqual(retryOf(p).paths, []), so the case is non-vacuous.
- b = commitOn(p, 'refs/heads/main', {'src/a.txt': 'main a\n'}). gateRuns = rows(log).length.
- r = landRun(p, 'wt-resume-unmerged-2', {}, {...REVIEW, WT_GATE_LOG: log, WT_CLI_RECORD: rec}, {type: 'claude'}). The typed CLI forwards the prompt (mem:gotcha-postflight-worktree-clishim-drops-argv). Pre-flight merges main and conflicts on src/a.txt, the CLI writes nothing, and the completion keeps the markers.
- One assert.deepEqual with tail(r.log). It expects:
  - promptOf(rec) === 'LANDING-CONFLICT: src/a.txt';
  - mainOf(p) === b;
  - revOf(p.W, 'MERGE_HEAD') === b;
  - the markers are still in W/src/a.txt;
  - r.log includes '[WARN] MOE_WORKTREE_UNRESOLVED_CONFLICT';
  - the last unlanded(p) entry is [outcome, unlandedReason, conflictPaths] = ['unlanded', 'conflict', ['src/a.txt']];
  - retryOf(p).paths deep-equals ['src/a.txt'];
  - rows(log).length === gateRuns, because the refusal happens at L2, before the gate.

Error handling: on failure each assertion message names its run, and the case leaves no extra fixture state. Reuse the existing helpers (repo, landRun, commitOn, gateCmd, retryOf, unlanded, promptOf, rows, tail, REVIEW, LANDS); add no new helper unless both cases need it.
